  "diagrams": {
    "hld": {
      "title": "High-Level Design",
      "mermaid": "flowchart TD\n  subgraph Firmware[\"Firmware\"]\n    app[\"Climate application<br/>firmware/app/app.c: app_start\"]\n    climate[\"Climate sampling policy<br/>climate_service_poll\"]\n    dhtport[\"DHT22 timing and frame capture<br/>platforms/stm32/platform_dht22.c\"]\n    i2cadapter[\"I2C scan and transfer adapter<br/>platforms/stm32/platform_i2c1.c\"]\n    logger[\"Log formatting<br/>firmware/utils/logger/logger.c\"]\n    uartadapter[\"UART logging adapter<br/>platforms/stm32/platform_logger.c\"]\n  end\n  subgraph BoardIO[\"Board I/O\"]\n    dht[\"DHT22 data line<br/>PB4\"]\n    tim3[\"Edge timing counter<br/>TIM3, 1 MHz\"]\n    i2c[\"I2C1 bus<br/>PB8 SCL, PB9 SDA\"]\n    usart[\"USART2 serial device<br/>TX PA2, RX PA3#59; 115200 baud\"]\n    console[\"ST-LINK Virtual COM Port<br/>UART console\"]\n  end\n  app -->|climate_service_init / climate_service_poll| climate\n  climate -->|climate_port_init / climate_port_read| dhtport\n  dhtport -->|HAL_GPIO_Init / HAL_GPIO_ReadPin / HAL_GPIO_WritePin| dht\n  dhtport -->|TIM3 counter capture#59; HAL_TIM_Base_Start| tim3\n  app -->|i2c_bus_init / i2c_bus_scan| i2cadapter\n  i2cadapter -->|HAL_I2C_Init / HAL_I2C_IsDeviceReady| i2c\n  app -->|LOGI / LOGE| logger\n  logger -->|logger_platform_write| uartadapter\n  app -->|platform_uart2_write climate frame| uartadapter\n  uartadapter -->|HAL_UART_Transmit| usart\n  usart -->|ST-LINK VCP| console",
      "authored_by_model": true,
      "node_notes": {
        "i2c": "The application initializes and scans the shared I2C1 bus; its pins are PB8 SCL and PB9 SDA. firmware/platforms/stm32/platform_i2c1.c configures them as alternate-function open-drain pins.",
        "tim3": "TIM3 supplies the free-running microsecond counter used to measure DHT22 pulse widths. firmware/platforms/stm32/platform_dht22.c configures a 1 MHz counter and reads it during frame capture.",
        "dhtport": "This STM32 adapter switches PB4 between open-drain low drive and input, captures the DHT22 response with TIM3, and decodes the resulting frame. The evidence is HAL_GPIO_Init, HAL_GPIO_ReadPin, HAL_GPIO_WritePin, and TIM3 setup in firmware/platforms/stm32/platform_dht22.c.",
        "dht": "The DHT22 shares its single-wire data line with the MCU on PB4, driven low and released to input by the platform adapter. The pin binding is APP_DHT22_GPIO_PORT and APP_DHT22_DATA_PIN in firmware/configs/app_config.h.",
        "logger": "This module formats tagged log messages before passing them to the platform writer. Its logger_platform_write call is implemented in firmware/utils/logger/logger.c.",
        "app": "The application initializes the I2C bus, scans it, starts climate sampling, and reports readings. Its startup and polling behavior are implemented by app_start in firmware/app/app.c.",
        "i2cadapter": "This adapter initializes I2C1 and performs the address sweep requested during application startup. Its HAL_I2C_Init and HAL_I2C_IsDeviceReady calls are in firmware/platforms/stm32/platform_i2c1.c.",
        "usart": "USART2 carries the formatted application and logger output at 115200 baud. firmware/platforms/stm32/platform_uart2.c binds TX to PA2 and RX to PA3 and transmits with HAL_UART_Transmit.",
        "uartadapter": "This platform bridge routes logger output to the UART2 adapter, while app_start also uses platform_uart2_write for the climate frame. The bridge is in firmware/platforms/stm32/platform_logger.c and the direct write is in firmware/app/app.c.",
        "climate": "This service enforces the minimum DHT22 sampling interval and maps port outcomes into climate statuses. The application calls climate_service_init and climate_service_poll from firmware/services/climate_service.c.",
        "console": "The UART adapter is documented as connecting USART2 to the NUCLEO-G070RB ST-LINK Virtual COM Port. This is the physical destination for UART logging in firmware/platforms/stm32/platform_uart2.c."
      }
    },
    "lld": {
      "title": "Low-Level Design (Firmware Workflow)",
      "mermaid": "flowchart TD\n  subgraph app_start[\"app_start task — firmware/app/app.c\"]\n    initbus[\"Initialize shared I2C bus<br/>firmware/app/app.c:79\"]\n    busok{\"I2C initialization succeeded — firmware/app/app.c:79\"}\n    initfail[\"Log I2C initialization failure<br/>firmware/app/app.c:81\"]\n    scan[\"Scan I2C addresses and report acknowledgements<br/>firmware/app/app.c:85\"]\n    scanok{\"I2C scan succeeded — firmware/app/app.c:85\"}\n    scanfail[\"Log I2C scan failure<br/>firmware/app/app.c:91\"]\n    initclimate[\"Initialize climate service and DHT22 port<br/>firmware/app/app.c:99\"]\n    climateok{\"Climate initialization succeeded — firmware/app/app.c:99\"}\n    climatefail[\"Log failure and remain in fatal loop<br/>firmware/app/app.c:102\"]\n    poll[\"Poll climate service<br/>firmware/app/app.c:108\"]\n    readok{\"Climate reading is valid — firmware/app/app.c:110\"}\n    report[\"Log temperature and humidity#59; send climate frame<br/>firmware/app/app.c:113\"]\n    readfail[\"Invalidate reading and log read failure<br/>firmware/app/app.c:137\"]\n    initbus -->  busok\n    busok -->|yes| scan\n    busok -->|no| initfail\n    scan -->  scanok\n    scanok -->|yes| initclimate\n    scanok -->|no| scanfail\n    scanfail -->  initclimate\n    initclimate -->  climateok\n    climateok -->|yes| poll\n    climateok -->|no| climatefail\n    poll -->  readok\n    readok -->|yes| report\n    readok -->|no| readfail\n    report -->|poll again#59; DHT22 sampling interval 2000 ms| poll\n    readfail -->|poll again#59; DHT22 sampling interval 2000 ms| poll\n  end",
      "authored_by_model": true,
      "node_notes": {
        "climatefail": "A DHT22 initialization failure is logged and keeps the application in a non-returning loop. The failure handling is in firmware/app/app.c.",
        "initfail": "The application logs an I2C1 initialization error and returns if bus setup fails. This failure path is in firmware/app/app.c.",
        "scanok": "This branch distinguishes an unsuccessful scan from a completed sweep. app_report_i2c_scan logs a failure or reports scan results in firmware/app/app.c.",
        "scanfail": "A failed scan is logged, after which startup continues to climate-service initialization. This path is in firmware/app/app.c.",
        "report": "On success, the application logs the temperature and humidity and sends a formatted CLIMATE frame over UART2. The reporting and platform_uart2_write call are in firmware/app/app.c.",
        "initbus": "app_start initializes the shared I2C bus before performing the address scan. The call and its status check are in firmware/app/app.c.",
        "busok": "This branch handles the return status from i2c_bus_init. A failure is logged and returns from app_start, while success proceeds to the scan in firmware/app/app.c.",
        "readfail": "On a failed poll, the application marks the reading invalid and logs the climate status. This error path is in firmware/app/app.c.",
        "poll": "The application repeatedly calls climate_service_poll to obtain a due DHT22 reading. The service enforces the configured 2000 ms minimum interval in firmware/services/climate_service.c.",
        "initclimate": "The application initializes the climate service after the bus scan. climate_service_init reaches the DHT22 platform initializer through firmware/services/climate_service.c and firmware/platforms/stm32/platform_dht22.c.",
        "climateok": "This branch checks the climate-service initialization result. On failure, the application logs the status and enters its fatal infinite loop in firmware/app/app.c.",
        "readok": "The application branches on CLIMATE_STATUS_OK to decide whether to report the reading or invalidate it and log an error. This check is in firmware/app/app.c.",
        "scan": "The application requests an I2C address sweep and reports the acknowledged addresses and NACK count. The scan and reporting routine is app_report_i2c_scan in firmware/app/app.c."
      }
